## 🗄️ Database Schema (Prisma)

```prisma
model Service {
  id          String   @id @default(cuid())
  title       String
  slug        String   @unique
  description String
  content     String   @db.Text    // Rich text / markdown
  icon        String?              // Lucide icon name
  imageUrl    String?
  featured    Boolean  @default(false)
  published   Boolean  @default(false)
  order       Int      @default(0)
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt   DateTime @updatedAt
}

model AdminUser {
  id        String   @id @default(cuid())
  email     String   @unique
  password  String                // bcrypt hashed
  name      String?
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
}
```

---

## 🌐 Public Website Sections

### 1. Landing Page (`/`)

Build a single-page layout with smooth scroll anchors:

**Hero Section**
- Full-viewport height
- Headline: *"Your Journey to the World Starts Here"*
- Subtext: *"Zayan Travels — Expert visa consulting for 50+ countries"*
- Two CTAs: "Explore Services" (primary) + "Contact Us" (outline)
- Subtle animated background: floating passport stamps or world map SVG with Framer Motion
- Scroll indicator arrow

**Why Choose Us** (3–4 icon cards)
- Fast Processing, Expert Guidance, High Success Rate, 24/7 Support

**Services Preview** (fetched from DB, published only, max 6)
- Card grid with service title, short description, icon, and "Learn More" link

**Google Reviews Section**
- Pull via `/api/reviews` which proxies Google Places API (New)
- Display: reviewer name, star rating, relative date, text (truncated to 180 chars)
- Auto-scrolling carousel (Framer Motion drag-to-scroll + autoplay)
- "Powered by Google" badge (required by Google branding policy)

**CTA Banner**
- "Ready to Apply? Let's Make It Happen" with contact button

### 2. About Page (`/about`)
- Agency story, founding year, mission statement
- Team section (static, hardcoded for now with placeholder avatars)
- Stats: countries covered, visas processed, years of experience

### 3. Services Page (`/services`)
- Dynamic grid fetched from DB (`published: true`, sorted by `order`)
- Each card: icon, title, description, CTA to contact
- No individual service detail pages needed (simplified scope)

### 4. Contact Page (`/contact`)
- Fields: Full Name, Email, Phone, Country of Destination, Message
- Zod validation on both client (RHF) and server (API route)
- On submit → POST `/api/contact` → Resend email to agency inbox
- Success toast, error handling, rate limiting via Vercel KV or simple in-memory

---

## 🔐 Admin Dashboard (`/dashboard`)

**Auth**
- NextAuth.js v5 Credentials provider
- Passwords hashed with bcrypt (12 rounds)
- Session stored in JWT (httpOnly cookie)
- `middleware.ts` protects all `/dashboard/*` routes — redirect to `/login` if unauthenticated
- Simple `/login` page (email + password)

**Dashboard Home**
- Stats cards: Total Services, Published, Drafts
- Quick-action buttons

**Services CRUD**
- List table: title, status (published badge), order, created date, actions (Edit / Delete)
- New Service form fields:
  - Title (auto-generates slug)
  - Short Description (max 160 chars)
  - Content (textarea — markdown)
  - Icon (select from preset Lucide icons list)
  - Image Upload (Uploadthing)
  - Featured toggle
  - Published toggle
  - Display Order (number)
- Edit page pre-fills form
- Delete with confirmation modal
- Drag-to-reorder rows (optional, use `@dnd-kit/core`)
- All mutations use optimistic updates via React Query

