## 🎨 Design System

**Brand Palette**
```css
--brand-primary: #1B4FD8;      /* Deep royal blue — trust, authority */
--brand-secondary: #F59E0B;    /* Warm amber — energy, optimism */
--brand-dark: #0F172A;         /* Near-black slate */
--brand-surface: #F8FAFC;      /* Off-white background */
--brand-muted: #64748B;        /* Secondary text */
```

**Typography**
- Display: `Plus Jakarta Sans` (bold headings)
- Body: `Inter` (readable paragraphs)
- Load via `next/font/google`

**Component Conventions**
- All `ui/` components accept a `className` prop for overrides
- Use `cva` (class-variance-authority) for variant-based components (Button, Badge)
- Consistent spacing scale from Tailwind (no arbitrary values unless necessary)

---

## ✅ Code Quality Requirements

- `"use client"` only where necessary — default to React Server Components
- All data fetching in server components or API routes (no client-side fetching of sensitive data)
- `loading.tsx` and `error.tsx` for each route segment
- `generateMetadata()` on every public page (title, description, OG image)
- Responsive: mobile-first, tested at 375px, 768px, 1280px
- Accessibility: semantic HTML, ARIA labels on interactive elements, keyboard nav
- Environment variables validated at startup with Zod (`lib/env.ts`)
- No `any` types — use proper interfaces and generics throughout
- ESLint + Prettier configured, husky pre-commit hook

---

## 📋 Completion & Commit Rules

- **Complete every section** — no placeholders, stubs, or TODO markers left behind. Every section of the project brief must be fully implemented before moving on.
- **Complete every page** — every route (public, admin, API) must be fully functional, responsive, and accessible. No page may be left as a shell or skeleton.
- **Complete every function** — every function, hook, and component must have a real, working implementation with proper types, error handling, and edge cases covered.
- **15-word commits** — every git commit message must be exactly 15 words or fewer, concise and descriptive of the change (e.g., `feat: add service CRUD with optimistic updates`).
- **Verify before commit** — run lint, type-check, and tests before committing; never commit broken or incomplete work.
- **One feature per commit** — keep commits focused and atomic; do not bundle unrelated changes together.

